# map!: key-to-value storage.
# Origin: confirmed against R3 3.22.1, driven by Rebol's own test suite.
#
# Added because it was the largest single thing missing. series-test.r3 and
# evaluation-test.r3 hold 1,959 assertions between them and both stopped at
# the first #[...] literal.
#
# A map is not a series. It has no position, so NEXT and FIRST mean nothing
# on one, and LENGTH? counts pairs rather than items. Reading a key it has
# not got gives NONE rather than raising, which is the opposite of an object
# and the same as a series position past the end: a map is asked about keys
# it may not have, and an object is asked for fields it should have.

# --- Reading one -------------------------------------------

--- id maps/a-hash-bracket-literal-is-a-map
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- note The brackets used to mean construction syntax in R3-Alpha. They
--- note were reused rather than freed up.
--- code
type? #[a: 1]
--- result
#(map!)

--- id maps/an-empty-map-literal
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
type? #[]
--- result
#(map!)

--- id maps/a-map-can-be-made-from-a-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
type? make map! [a: 1 b: 2]
--- result
#(map!)

--- id maps/keys-need-not-be-words
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- note #[1 2] has the integer 1 as a key, which is what separates a map
--- note from an object: a map's keys are values, not names.
--- code
type? #[1 2]
--- result
#(map!)

# --- Getting values out -------------------------------------

--- id maps/a-path-reads-a-key
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
m: #[a: 1]
m/a
--- result
1

--- id maps/a-key-that-is-not-there-gives-none
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- note The boundary that separates a map from an object. An object raises
--- note invalid-path for a field it has not got; a map answers NONE.
--- code
m: #[a: 1]
m/zz
--- result
_

--- id maps/select-reads-a-key-too
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
select #[a: 1] 'a
--- result
1

--- id maps/select-on-a-missing-key-is-none
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
select #[a: 1] 'zz
--- result
_

# --- How big ------------------------------------------------

--- id maps/length-counts-pairs
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- note Pairs, not items. A block of the same source would be four long.
--- code
length? #[a: 1 b: 2]
--- result
2

--- id maps/an-empty-map-has-no-length
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
length? #[]
--- result
0

# --- Equality and molding -----------------------------------

--- id maps/two-maps-with-the-same-pairs-are-equal
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
equal? #[a: 1] #[a: 1]
--- result
#(true)

--- id maps/maps-with-different-values-are-not-equal
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
equal? #[a: 1] #[a: 2]
--- result
#(false)

--- id maps/an-empty-map-molds-on-one-line
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- note The degenerate case is the only one that does not break the line.
--- code
mold #[]
--- result
"#[]"

# --- Changing one -------------------------------------------

--- id maps/put-adds-a-key
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
m: #[]
put m 'a 1
m/a
--- result
1

--- id maps/put-replaces-an-existing-key
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- note A key appears once however many times it is put, which is the
--- note invariant that makes a map a map.
--- code
m: #[a: 1]
put m 'a 2
length? m
--- result
1

--- id maps/keys-of-gives-the-keys-as-a-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
keys-of #[a: 1 b: 2]
--- result
[a b]

--- id maps/values-of-gives-the-values-as-a-block
--- origin confirmed against R3 3.22.1
--- requires map
--- code
values-of #[a: 1 b: 2]
--- result
[1 2]
